  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating the Potential for Tension and Conflict in Areas Impacted by the Refugee Influx in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to mitigate tensions and possible causes of conflict and contribute to creating an environment for improved stability and social cohesion in towns and villages neighbouring the Um Rakuba camp in Gedaref, Sudan. It does so to support crisis-affected refugees, migrants, and hosting communities through: (1) Providing access to basic services and responding to community-prioritized needs, improving local capacities to ensure there is sustainable access to services for local populations; (2) Promoting social cohesion by improving opportunities for dialogue, positive social interaction; and (3) Providing and enhancing livelihood and employment opportunities to reduce vulnerabilities and promote socio-economic development.</narrative>
  </description>
